WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.492
A useful architecture rule is to promote stable meaning into persistent objects.

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:11.557
If many consumers agree on what a patient-admission row means, that can become a view.

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:17.927
If one report uses a temporary thirty-day threshold, keep that logic in the report.

00:00:17.927 --> 00:00:24.017
If a summary is expensive and reused frequently, materialization may be appropriate.

00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:28.102
Do not turn every query into a database object.

00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:32.167
Choose the smallest reusable object that matches the need.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:37.572
A CTE is local to one query, a view centralizes live logic,

00:00:37.572 --> 00:00:40.857
and a materialized view persists a snapshot.

00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:46.802
Promote logic into shared objects when it is stable, reused, and worth governing as part of the analytical

00:00:46.802 --> 00:00:48.606
architecture.
